# handbrake

The agent can drive. Spend is the human's decision, one change at a time.

1. Reads are free. Pausing is always allowed. Creates are fine: they land paused or as unpublished drafts. Never pass `status: ACTIVE` on a create.
2. Before any activation, budget or status change, run `node scripts/handbrake.js explain <tool> '<json>'` (copy `handbrake.js` from https://github.com/codegobrrrr9/handbrake) and show the human the one-line summary. Do not call the write until they say yes to that exact change.
3. Caps in `.handbrake/policy.json` are the human's. Never edit anything under `.handbrake/`; never split a change to get under a cap.
4. Save insights to JSON and run `node scripts/handbrake.js audit <file>`; each flag is a proposal, not an action.
5. End every done message with the line from `node scripts/handbrake.js status`. Never say "live" unless the ledger shows the write succeeded.
